# Keep LF on the files a Linux runner executes as shell.
#
# core.autocrlf=true (the usual Windows setting) already stores LF in the
# repository, so this is belt and braces - but the failure it prevents is a
# nasty one. The publish job's `run:` blocks are bash, and a CRLF heredoc
# terminator (`EOF\r`) does not match `EOF`, so the script runs to end-of-file
# and dies with a syntax error that says nothing about line endings.
#
# Deliberately narrow: no `* text=auto`, so nothing else in the tree is
# renormalised.
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
